      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OCEAN TSUNAMI (3) sets the standard after winning by a nose in Class 3 at Randwick, and she now comes back from Saturday company with a strong profile at this track and distance. Her Rosehill fifth before that had enough interference to be more valuable than the margin suggests, so she looks the horse to beat third-up. GRANDINI (6) has not threatened in two runs this campaign, but both were stronger assignments, including a BM82 fifth at this venue, and her distance record plus the 3kg claim keep her right in the contest. ALABAMA BLITZ (7) has to rebound from a last at Newcastle, yet her prior second at this track showed she can be competitive when ridden more patiently. Winkers first time can do the trick. DISCO PRINCE (4) was at big odds when second to WANDJAD in BM66 grade and has a sound each-way profile if he repeats that effort. Ready for this trip.",
